 (3,'8','Canada DC base path: FEL 269 TWh (2040) is ~2x the sourced frontier (220 TWh). Re-base in v7, or run 8A as a below-base case?','Otherwise the "frontier" scenario cuts demand.'),
 (4,'3 / 12','Should DC variants come from the FEL demand model presets (dc_scenario high/low) or from the external-anchored paths proposed here?','Consistency with SE-published FEL numbers vs traceability to public forecasts.'),
 (5,'2','Accept flat electrolysis load for a first run, or invest in a flexible electrolyser formulation (M-L effort)?','At 333 TWh flat the model over-builds firm capacity.'),
